#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063944 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064344 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9564e999-9aa4-5f44-bc9b-d2aad049900a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "931ca260-f460-5126-a410-e7e929c16dd7" :question/math-academy-id "e-13006" :question/problem "Given that $12 - 5m = 3m$, what is the value of $m$?" :question/worked-solution "We must bring all variables to one side of the equation and all constants to the other side.\n\nNotice that we have $-5m$ on the left-hand side and $3m$ on the right-hand side. Since the variable on the right-hand side has a larger coefficient, let's bring all the variables to this side.\n\nThe first step is to remove the $-5m$ from the left-hand side. We do this by adding ${\\color{blue}5m}$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n12 - 5m &= 3m \\\\\n12 - 5m + 5m &= 3m + 5m \\\\\n12 &= 8m\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide both sides of the equation by $8$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n12 &= 8m \\\\\n\\frac{12}{8} &= \\frac{8m}{8} \\\\\n\\frac{3}{2} &= \\frac{8m}{8} \\\\\n\\frac{3}{2} &= m \\\\\nm &= \\frac{3}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063945 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064345 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "24a6a642-f1c3-5550-b40e-78fc6730bcf3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Three-Step Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "615f4a8c-a7d7-5533-badc-fc3d12678c95" :question/math-academy-id "e-13007" :question/problem "Solve the equation $3x-12 = 5x + 8$." :question/worked-solution "We must bring all variables to one side of the equation and all constants to the other side.\n\nNotice that we have $3x$ on the left-hand side and $5x$ on the right-hand side. Since the variable on the right-hand side has a larger coefficient, let's bring all the variables to this side.\n\nThe first step is to remove the $3x$ from the left-hand side of the equation. We do this by subtracting ${\\color{blue}3x}$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x - 12 &= 5x + 8 \\\\\n3x - 12 - 3x &= 5x + 8 - 3x \\\\\n- 12 &= 2x + 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we remove the $8$ from the right-hand side. We do this by subtracting ${\\color{red}8}$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12 &= 2x + 8 \\\\\n- 12 - 8 &= 2x + 8 - 8 \\\\\n- 20 &= 2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide both sides of the equation by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-20 &= 2x \\\\\n\\frac{-20}{2} &= \\frac{2x}{2} \\\\\n- 10 &= \\frac{2x}{2} \\\\\n- 10 &= x \\\\\nx &= -10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063946 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064346 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75d27dfc-1297-5045-bedd-10e171209430" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/id #uuid "afb93968-87c1-5d28-8922-8143e6db77c7" :question/math-academy-id "e-13008" :question/problem "Solve for $t$ where $2(t+3)= 5t-3$." :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses on the left-hand-side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(t + 3) &= 5t - 3 \\\\\n2 \\cdot t + 2 \\cdot 3 &= 5t - 3 \\\\\n2t + 6 &= 5t - 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we must now bring all variables to one side of the equation and all constants to the other side.\n\nNotice that we have $2t$ on the left-hand side and $5t$ on the right-hand side. Since the variable on the right-hand side has a larger coefficient, let's bring all the variables to this side.\n\nThe first step is to remove the $2t$ from the left-hand side of the equation. We do this by subtracting ${\\color{blue}2t}$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2t + 6 &= 5t - 3 \\\\\n2t + 6 - 2t &= 5t - 3 - 2t \\\\\n6 &= 3t - 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we remove the $-3$ from the right-hand side. We do this by adding ${\\color{red}3}$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6 &= 3t - 3 \\\\\n6 + 3 &= 3t - 3 + 3 \\\\\n9 &= 3t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide both sides of the equation by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n9 &= 3t \\\\\n\\frac{9}{3} &= \\frac{3t}{3} \\\\\n3 &= \\frac{3t}{3} \\\\\n3 &= t \\\\\nt &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
